Description: Nodes for planning experiments in a trama graph: a declarative
    design node that builds and randomizes completely randomized, randomized
    block, Latin square, factorial (with or without confounding in blocks),
    fractional factorial 2^(k-p), central composite, split-plot, strip-plot,
    balanced incomplete block, repeated measures, crossover (Williams) and
    multi-site designs, with every factor's role, unit of assignment and
    randomization scope made explicit. The plan carries its metadata and
    becomes a plain table for the analysis nodes of trama.models. Builds on
    trama.data for tables, trama.view for plots and trama.models for
    the fitted models that the analysis nodes read.
